{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it","id":1160409,"title":"GURPS Werewolf is it worth it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-18T20:57:31-08:00","id":1160409,"title":"GURPS Werewolf is it worth it?","content":"So i have this love hate relationship with Apocalypse. I love the setting to death but i hate the mechanics, i hate OWoD combat as i think is where the system shits the bed but oh boy some of the design choices of Werewolf are specially rotten.<br /> <br /> My issues are damage rolls.<br /> <br /> Purebreed is the worst mechanic ever designed in gaming.<br /> <br /> Rage breaks an already clunky system.<br /> <br /> Gift go from OP to completely useless and is a mess of complication with the whole &quot;Gnosis/rage&quot; expenditure.<br /> <br /> Regeneration is needlesly obtuse.<br /> <br /> So many of the problems i can fix. Replace damage rolls with Attack vs Defense roll and the soak and increase health by 5 + stamina. Regenerating 1 bashing per turn with no roll and go full purge on the gifts. That said multiaction rage and the Gnosis/Rage divide is kinda hard to mess with.<br /> <br /> But then i tough about GURPS werewolf. I read that GURPS is a fairly solid system so i am wondering for those who try it. How was it? Whats the good and the bad system wise? Can it offer me a way to run Apocalypse without the issues i find problematic in the current system?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T07:53:44-08:00","id":1160509,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it#post1160409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My issues are damage rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is your issue?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it#post1160409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Purebreed is the worst mechanic ever designed in gaming.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Why ?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it#post1160409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rage breaks an already clunky system.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">How so ?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it#post1160409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gift go from OP to completely useless and is a mess of complication with the whole &quot;Gnosis/rage&quot; expenditure.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Give me an example of your experience to this issue.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it#post1160409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regeneration is needlesly obtuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 11-19-2017, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T10:05:52-08:00","id":1160544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it#post1160409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So i have this love hate relationship with Apocalypse. I love the setting to death but i hate the mechanics, i hate OWoD combat as i think is where the system shits the bed but oh boy some of the design choices of Werewolf are specially rotten.<br /> <br /> My issues are damage rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>GURPS is still going to have damage roll issues, mind you. Especially at higher dice values, like with explosions, where you could be facing, say, 6dx200 at ground zero of 50 lbs of TNT going off (#d always means #d6; the system only uses six-siders). Given how heavy weapons and high explosives turn soft targets into hamburger, you're going to need to play with the system to keep that under control.<br /> <br /> For reference, an assault rifle does about 7d and it only takes ten points of damage to seriously injure the average person and make the lose consciousness; anything more risks death, which is automatic either if you hit someone in an area that would kill them (i.e. slitting a throat or shooting them through the heart) or at 60 points of damage. 100 points of damage results in complete bodily destruction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Purebreed is the worst mechanic ever designed in gaming. </div> </div> </div>First off, that's not really a combat concern. Secondly, I'm pretty sure that there are lots of D&amp;D mechanics, original Mage magick rules, and all of FATAL to go through first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rage breaks an already clunky system. </div> </div> </div>Extra attacks are a hell of a drug, but you'll also get them in GURPS. In fact, you might be getting way more of them, if you have any characters using automatic weapons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gift go from OP to completely useless and is a mess of complication with the whole &quot;Gnosis/rage&quot; expenditure. </div> </div> </div>I don't really mind the Gnosis and Rage interference, but otherwise, yes. GURPS will actually solve this problem to some extent, as Gifts are going to end up as constructed powers using point values.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regeneration is needlesly obtuse. </div> </div> </div>Are we talking the Stamina roll to recover lethal here? Because I do hate that. Though, in GURPS, regeneration is typically a book-keeping burden, since you'll be recovering 1 HP/s, and turns are one second, only you'll occasionally need to ready a weapon before using it if it's too unwieldy...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So many of the problems i can fix. Replace damage rolls with Attack vs Defense roll and the soak and increase health by 5 + stamina. Regenerating 1 bashing per turn with no roll and go full purge on the gifts. That said multiaction rage and the Gnosis/Rage divide is kinda hard to mess with.<br /> <br /> But then i tough about GURPS werewolf. I read that GURPS is a fairly solid system so i am wondering for those who try it. How was it? Whats the good and the bad system wise? Can it offer me a way to run Apocalypse without the issues i find problematic in the current system? </div> </div> </div>GURPS is solid for its wargaming roots, but you're going to need to get 1) a copy of the core book, which may be rather pricey, and the only pdfs on Drivethru are for a new edition, and 2) a fairly large hexsheet, since it relies heavily on positioning, and you'll have to tinker with the old GURPS Werewolf: the Apocalypse release a bit if you want to use any of the new stuff that was written for 4e (as GURPS W:tA was written for a much earlier iteration of 4e). Among difficulties you'll face, in addition to the ones above, are changing hit point totals (either as part of a template or because GURPS 4e bases HP on Strength), Crinos potentially being way less capable because of the way different lifting charts work, keeping track of damage types under different situations, random hit locations for anyone who doesn't aim at a specific part, and having to stat up spirits with actual stats instead of Rage, Gnosis, Willpower, and Power/Essence. Also, defenses may be a bit more difficult to manage, since IIRC you'll be looking at margins of success rather than how many dice come up a certain number.<br /> <br /> Also, the skill list is an 80s skill list, often differentiating various concentrations of skills into slashes of general category and tech level category. Unless you use 4e's Bang! Skills to cover multiple areas, you're going to be in a hell of Mechanic/Cars/TL 7, Mechanic/Cars/TL 8, Guns/ Pistols/ TL 5 (antique old west pistols), Guns/Pistols/TL 6 (early 20th century pistols), Guns/Pistols/ TL 7 (post mid-20th century to lateish 20th century), and Guns/Pistols/TL 8 (anything that's new). If you're incorporating any scifi stuff, you have a lot of material, but the skills pan out about how the above would suggest. Rock solid simulationism has downsides, and it comes in the form of a default sprawling skill list, as well as the question of how to convert animal forms; GURPS W:tA has conversions for the numbers for Garou forms, of course, but Lupus Attribute modifiers are very different from wolf Attributes. In some cases, such as with Gurahl, using the stat bonuses might leave a character substantially under-powered in 3e (in 4e, you determine the Strength of a large beast by taking the cube root of its weight in pounds and doubling the result, round up.<br /> <br /> (You can get pdfs of older stuff on Warehouse 23, the official site for SJ Games, but I have heard complaints about the quality of service more recently, so registrant and buyer beware.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 11-19-2017, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T12:44:09-08:00","id":1160607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160509#post1160509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is your issue?</div> </div> </div> </div><u><b>Damage rolls</b></u><br /> <br /> Simply put they arent fun/satisfying for neither attacker or defender. Many times the situation of a very good attack roll get turned into nothing because of bad luck on the damage roll. One would say that's the same that a very good attack roll getting reduced to nothing by a defense roll. But is not the same, in the former, your PC (the defender) didn't avoid damage because of any ability or good roll on his part but just because the other rolled a shitty roll.<br /> <br /> Using a similar system in Shadowrun 5th, you got an attack roll vs defense roll and the soak for the defender and it tends to feel better and not as frustrating as there is a better flow of back and forth between attacker and defender.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160509#post1160509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Why ?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><u><b>Pure Breed</b></u><br /> <br /> Because its a god stat worse than generation in Masquerade. Its add its rating to social rolls challenges against Garou and Kinfolk. It adds to power that uses social stats and as a big chunk of garou politics are handled by challenges (that include raising rank and fights) it ends up being a cheap background that doubles as both a social, supernatural and combat stat.<br /> <br /> The fact that it only works on Garou and Kinfolk is almost irrelevant as 90% of Garou only interact with those. Even their society is constructed in such a way to allow them that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160509#post1160509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">How so ?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><u><b>Rage and </b></u><u><b>multiaction</b></u><u><b>. </b></u><br /> <br /> Simply put multiaction breaks the system. And a character that can dish 3 attacks per turn breaks the system massively.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160509#post1160509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Give me an example of your experience to this issue.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><b><u>Gifts that go from OP to useless.</u></b><br /> <br /> Tons of examples so I am not gonna touch on that many. A big part is OWoD clunky system juggling 3 variables (+/- difficulties, +/- dice, more success required) and never deciding when each applies. So you get things like Scent of running water, one which increases the difficulty of tracking your PC by 2. And Blur of the milky eye which one rolls manipulation + Stealth (difficulty 8) and each success increases the opponent's perception roll by 1. Both of which are rank 1. The former is kinda useless when you got the latter.<br /> <br /> But then you got things like Rank 2 Children of Gaia gift &quot;Spellbinding Oration&quot; which is the worse of both part of the previous 2 gifts. Requiring a roll but only reducing by 2 (regardless of success) on social rolls.<br /> <br /> Then you got the Children of Gaia list which is various iterations of &quot;don't frenzy&quot; which makes them redundant as each new renders the previously obsolete. Arhouns have a gift &quot;Spirit of the frey&quot; rank 2 that gives you +10 to initiative and another +10 if one spend gnosis.<br /> <br /> Couple with the whole Gnosis/Rage divide it generates an annoying bookkeeping on &quot;what gift can/can't use this turn&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160509#post1160509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so ?</div> </div> </div> </div><u><b>Poorly designed regeneration.</b></u><br /> <br /> First Werewolf regenerate 1 bashing per turn or 1 lethal if he passes a stamina (diff 8) roll. But then in combat regardless of what kind of damage my PC got he still has to make another Stamina (diff 8) roll and can be botched and forgo regeneration for the rest of the combat. Then there is the whole cluster fuck of what you can and cant soak because you can soak silver while in Breed form but can soak anything lethal and viceversa.<br /> <br /> All of this is poor design and could have been easily solved (and was done so in forsaken) with. Silver always regenerate 1 bashing per turn, spend 1 gnosis to make it 1 lethal and eat Aggravated from lethal in all forms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160544#post1160544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, I'm pretty sure that there are lots of D&amp;D mechanics, original Mage magick rules, and all of FATAL to go through first.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. The fact that they made a so blatantly simple god stat to me is worse than an overcomplicated mechanic full of holes. But YMMV.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160544#post1160544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really mind the Gnosis and Rage interference, but otherwise, yes. GURPS will actually solve this problem to some extent, as Gifts are going to end up as constructed powers using point values.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160544#post1160544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the skill list is an 80s skill list, often differentiating various concentrations of skills into slashes of general category and tech level category. Unless you use 4e's Bang! Skills to cover multiple areas, you're going to be in a hell of Mechanic/Cars/TL 7, Mechanic/Cars/TL 8, Guns/ Pistols/ TL 5 (antique old west pistols), Guns/Pistols/TL 6 (early 20th century pistols), Guns/Pistols/ TL 7 (post mid-20th century to lateish 20th century), and Guns/Pistols/TL 8 (anything that's new). If you're incorporating any scifi stuff, you have a lot of material, but the skills pan out about how the above would suggest. Rock solid simulationism has downsides, and it comes in the form of a default sprawling skill list, as well as the question of how to convert animal forms; GURPS W:tA has conversions for the numbers for Garou forms, of course, but Lupus Attribute modifiers are very different from wolf Attributes. In some cases, such as with Gurahl, using the stat bonuses might leave a character substantially under-powered in 3e (in 4e, you determine the Strength of a large beast by taking the cube root of its weight in pounds and doubling the result, round up.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not so much of a problem I can just erase skill list and reduce them no problems as long as all skill rolll follow the same basic roll. And as i dont use changing breed in my game just Garou don't know how much the forms are gonna be a problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160544#post1160544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">GURPS is solid for its wargaming roots, but you're going to need to get 1) a copy of the core book, which may be rather pricey, and the only pdfs on Drivethru are for a new edition, and 2) a fairly large hexsheet, since it relies heavily on positioning, and you'll have to tinker with the old GURPS Werewolf: the Apocalypse release a bit if you want to use any of the new stuff that was written for 4e (as GURPS W:tA was written for a much earlier iteration of 4e). Among difficulties you'll face, in addition to the ones above, are changing hit point totals (either as part of a template or because GURPS 4e bases HP on Strength), Crinos potentially being way less capable because of the way different lifting charts work, keeping track of damage types under different situations, random hit locations for anyone who doesn't aim at a specific part, and having to stat up spirits with actual stats instead of Rage, Gnosis, Willpower, and Power/Essence. Also, defenses may be a bit more difficult to manage, since IIRC you'll be looking at margins of success rather than how many dice come up a certain number.<br /> <br /> GURPS is still going to have damage roll issues, mind you. Especially at higher dice values, like with explosions, where you could be facing, say, 6dx200 at ground zero of 50 lbs of TNT going off (#d always means #d6; the system only uses six-siders). Given how heavy weapons and high explosives turn soft targets into hamburger, you're going to need to play with the system to keep that under control.<br /> <br /> For reference, an assault rifle does about 7d and it only takes ten points of damage to seriously injure the average person and make the loose consciousness; anything more risks death, which is automatic either if you hit someone in an area that would kill them (i.e. slitting a throat or shooting them through the heart) or at 60 points of damage. 100 points of damage results in complete bodily destruction.<br /> <br /> Extra attacks are a hell of a drug, but you'll also get them in GURPS. In fact, you might be getting way more of them, if you have any characters using automatic weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>This does concern me though. I have a copy of the 2 4E cores and i found an used copy of GURPS werewolf (pretty banged up) so i was asking as i never read it. But yeah if it has the extra attack problems of OWoD i guess it is out.<br /> <br /> I guess I could just use Shadowrun 5th edition and just figure out a way to transplant gifts. I was toying with the idea of houseruling OWoD into &quot;attack roll (with strength) vs Defense roll and then soak and weapon giving you extra damage but boosting health to 5 + stamina ala NWoD but the whole Rage it seems difficult to mold into something not OP<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-19-2017, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T13:31:34-08:00","id":1160631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160607#post1160607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Damage rolls</b></u><br /> <br /> Simply put they arent fun/satisfying for neither attacker or defender. Many times the situation of a very good attack roll get turned into nothing because of bad luck on the damage roll. One would say that's the same that a very good attack roll getting reduced to nothing by a defense roll. But is not the same, in the former, your PC (the defender) didn't avoid damage because of any ability or good roll on his part but just because the other rolled a shitty roll.<br /> <br /> Using a similar system in Shadowrun 5th, you got an attack roll vs defense roll and the soak for the defender and it tends to feel better and not as frustrating as there is a better flow of back and forth between attacker and defender.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The only issue, I ever had in damage rolls pre W20 was the rediculously massive damage pools from added attack roll successes, I had blind grandpas with rifles shoooting down crinos garou with a single trigger pull. Or hamstring shots that ended up ripping appart the victim instead of a normal hamstring effect. But I found such cases extremely funny. Now there is the time issue, that indeed may tire up the group.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160607#post1160607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Pure Breed</b></u><br /> <br /> Because its a god stat worse than generation in Masquerade. Its add its rating to social rolls challenges against Garou and Kinfolk. It adds to power that uses social stats and as a big chunk of garou politics are handled by challenges (that include raising rank and fights) it ends up being a cheap background that doubles as both a social, supernatural and combat stat.<br /> <br /> The fact that it only works on Garou and Kinfolk is almost irrelevant as 90% of Garou only interact with those. Even their society is constructed in such a way to allow them that.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Why should you compare it to Masquerade anyway, it has no logic, Ascension also has Avatar background that they HAVE to take and thats highly demanding.<br /> The Pur Breed Background is indeed powerful stat among Garou, but it is also used in highly specific situations, like the ones you mentioned above, a campaign may not be only about Garou. So its more likely an ''or the height's or the depth's'' situation background, never had a problem with that.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160607#post1160607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Rage and </b></u><u><b>multiaction</b></u><u><b>. </b></u><br /> <br /> Simply put multiaction breaks the system. And a character that can dish 3 attacks per turn breaks the system massively.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Any character can do multi actions by breaking dice pools, if that is a problem for you then you prob should remove it entirely from your games. What do you mean by ''broken system''?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160607#post1160607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Gifts that go from OP to useless.</u></b><br /> <br /> Tons of examples so I am not gonna touch on that many. A big part is OWoD clunky system juggling 3 variables (+/- difficulties, +/- dice, more success required) and never deciding when each applies. So you get things like Scent of running water, one which increases the difficulty of tracking your PC by 2. And Blur of the milky eye which one rolls manipulation + Stealth (difficulty 8) and each success increases the opponent's perception roll by 1. Both of which are rank 1. The former is kinda useless when you got the latter.<br /> <br /> But then you got things like Rank 2 Children of Gaia gift &quot;Spellbinding Oration&quot; which is the worse of both part of the previous 2 gifts. Requiring a roll but only reducing by 2 (regardless of success) on social rolls.<br /> <br /> Then you got the Children of Gaia list which is various iterations of &quot;don't frenzy&quot; which makes them redundant as each new renders the previously obsolete. Arhouns have a gift &quot;Spirit of the frey&quot; rank 2 that gives you +10 to initiative and another +10 if one spend gnosis.<br /> <br /> Couple with the whole Gnosis/Rage divide it generates an annoying bookkeeping on &quot;what gift can/can't use this turn&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>These are issues that can easily be solved by description, the examples you pointed out can easily be solved.<br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Blur of the milky eye affects only sight, that means that you are still vulnerable to sounds, Scent of running water works on tracking, these are two completely different siruations, a character with heightened senses gifts can render useless the blur gift, coz he can easily spot the blured werewolf with his other senses, blur is a good gift for anyone except characters with other super senses, while Scent of running water will be way better on long run situations. The not frenzy situations need to let the Child of gaia vulnerable to attack in order to prevent frenzy, appart from that it is a gift most useful in social and challenge situations, and Spirit of the frey gnosis spend lasts for a turn that you cannot spend Rage for any reason, highly situational, well the +10 initiative is indeed a serious matter, but only in combat.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160607#post1160607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Poorly designed regeneration.</b></u><br /> <br /> First Werewolf regenerate 1 bashing per turn or 1 lethal if he passes a stamina (diff 8) roll. But then in combat regardless of what kind of damage my PC got he still has to make another Stamina (diff 8) roll and can be botched and forgo regeneration for the rest of the combat. Then there is the whole cluster fuck of what you can and cant soak because you can soak silver while in Breed form but can soak anything lethal and viceversa.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not a whole cluster, you can soak silver only if it is from a bludgeon weapon, like a spoon or blunt supper knife, you can't soak sharp blades or silver bullets, they do lethal in breed form, but they can kill you even if you don't shapeshift. The stamina roll can make the combat turn even longer but well it can be dramatic in some cases and add to a player's agony.<br /> See, it's easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 11-19-2017, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T15:31:19-08:00","id":1160666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160631#post1160631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]Why should you compare it to Masquerade anyway, it has no logic, Ascension also has Avatar background that they HAVE to take and thats highly demanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made the Generation comparison because is often tough as one of the bad mechanics in Masquerade. Avatar if I remember correctly (had a similar issue) but only applied to the expenditure of quiessence (though i could be wrong, don't have the book with me now) it wasn't a social, political and combat stat all rolled in one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160631#post1160631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Any character can do multi actions by breaking dice pools, if that is a problem for you then you prob should remove it entirely from your games. What do you mean by ''broken system''?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Breaking the dice pool was an incredible punishing mechanic for one (having to use the lower of the 4 stats involved). Is a problem when a character can use 4 multi-action that with no penalty to those.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160631#post1160631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are issues that can easily be solved by description, the examples you pointed out can easily be solved.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Blur of the milky eye affects only sight, that means that you are still vulnerable to sounds, Scent of running water works on tracking, these are two completely different situations, a character with heightened senses gifts can render useless the blur gift, coz he can easily spot the blurred werewolf with his other senses, blur is a good gift for anyone except characters with other super senses, while Scent of running water will be way better on long-run situations. The not frenzy situations need to let the Child of Gaia vulnerable to attack in order to prevent frenzy, apart from that it is a gift most useful in social and challenge situations, and Spirit of the frey gnosis spend lasts for a turn that you cannot spend Rage for any reason, highly situational, well the +10 initiative is indeed a serious matter, but only in combat.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Sorry, but first thats not how it works, it affects the perception stat which encompasses the 5 senses and applies to tracking. I don't get what you mean with &quot;Let the child of Gaia vulnerable to attack&quot; when i didn't mean a specific gift but a series of gift that do the same thing but render the previous ones redundant.<br /> <br /> And yes is an easy if taxing problem to solve just going through all the gift list and banning and fixing the redundant and/useless gifts which are more XP traps than anything else. Like the Gift to purify water.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160631#post1160631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a whole cluster, you can soak silver only if it is from a bludgeon weapon, like a spoon or blunt supper knife, you can't soak sharp blades or silver bullets, they do lethal in breed form, but they can kill you even if you don't shapeshift. The stamina roll can make the combat turn even longer but well it can be dramatic in some cases and add to a player's agony.<br /> See, it's easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I understand how it works that why I wrote how it works. My point is that how it works is needlessly convoluted and you have kept all of that in your mind in each combat. Instead of all of that<br /> <br /> &quot;Garou always regenerate 1 bashing per turn, spend 1 gnosis to make it 1 lethal and eat Aggravated from Silver in all forms. Soak lethal in all&quot; less than a whole line vs your 2 entire lines of text. That's a better design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-19-2017, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T15:53:09-08:00","id":1160673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160607#post1160607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know. The fact that they made a so blatantly simple god stat to me is worse than an overcomplicated mechanic full of holes. But YMMV.</div> </div> </div> </div>For all its faults, the Werewolf to Werewolf Conversion guidelines made it so that Pure Breed in Forsaken had a drawback of making Renown more difficult to get, because you had to put extra work into being a hero to look like you're building on your family legacy rather than riding its coattails. You could easily implement a system of &quot;reduce temporary Renown rewards across the board by half Pure Breed&quot; to give it a similar downside in Apocalypse. Also, it's nowhere near as broken as Generation. Nothing is as broken as Generation, even when you take into account the downside of being a target for Hungry Hungry Diablerists.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's good. </div> </div> </div>Also, some Gifts will have more combat utility than you might think - in ST, Speed of Thought doesn't really allow you to hit harder. In GURPS, increased move such as from Super Running can allow you to tackle or ram enemies for a potentially significant increase in damage. Fear the GURPS-played Silent Striders and Swara.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's not so much of a problem I can just erase skill list and reduce them no problems as long as all skill rolll follow the same basic roll. And as i dont use changing breed in my game just Garou don't know how much the forms are gonna be a problem. </div> </div> </div>Well, as I said, there's an in-built system for group-type skills in 4e. Guns! covers everything that Guns/Whatever/Whatever will.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This does concern me though. I have a copy of the 2 4E cores and i found an used copy of GURPS werewolf (pretty banged up) so i was asking as i never read it. But yeah if it has the extra attack problems of OWoD i guess it is out. </div> </div> </div>You'd have an easier time taking the extra attacks out of Werewolf as-is. You can mostly use the 4e cores with 3e stuff, though; there's a conversion pdf to help guide the process along.<br /> <br /> (Lasers are especially nasty, since they end up adding up all dice from all attacks to a single location for one big damage cluster instead of each rolling separately against armor, and in prior editions, they did impaling damage, which was doubled after subtracting DR. In 4e though, lasers do burning damage, which Garou would likely be able to resist much more ably when the time came to duke it out with near future-tech gadget antagonists.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess I could just use Shadowrun 5th edition and just figure out a way to transplant gifts. I was toying with the idea of houseruling OWoD into &quot;attack roll (with strength) vs Defense roll and then soak and weapon giving you extra damage but boosting health to 5 + stamina ala NWoD but the whole Rage it seems difficult to mold into something not OP </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't even use SR5 for SR. Edge is stupidly overpowered, especially given the existence of Limits in 5e. Even in past editions, Karma Pool was never a part of the rules that I liked all that much, so making it completely central and having it overcharge every roll that you make with it instead of being a set of second chances to avoid dying strikes me as a terrible mechanical decision.<br /> <br /> Another system that CGL makes, A Time of War (the BattleTech RPG), also has no-roll damage, if you're interested and haven't picked it up or passed on it already. Its Edge problems are a bit less than those of SR5, too, since it doesn't allow you to bypass all other traits and become the hero just from one point of it wagered before each roll. You could also model Crinos fairly well with power armor rules, at least in terms of how it can tear even tanks to pieces, given teamwork and time. You'd have to make some other rules to cover regeneration, but the Pay What You Want semi-joke pdf Nebula California could potentially help there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 11-19-2017, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T16:29:26-08:00","id":1160688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160544#post1160544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, that's not really a combat concern. Secondly, I'm pretty sure that there are lots of D&amp;D mechanics, original Mage magick rules, and all of FATAL to go through first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but I don't see many D&amp;D mechanics since 3rd edition being worse than most of WoD mechanics. If you think AD&amp;D, though, you didn't saw weird rules if you didn't saw TACH0. Unless it is FATAL...<br /> <br /> Now, <b>Saur Ops Specialist</b> already did a fine job describing how it will behave in GURPS. It is a nice system for its time, and you'll get rid of some problems, while having better tools to circumvent others (if you don't like multiple actions, implement other GURPS's mechanics to represent speed of action).<br /> <br /> But I think you'll be maybe better served by yet another system. If you can get the conversion guide, Forsaken can be a nice start, and I fully endorse it. But if you thought of GURPS, what about Mutants &amp; Masterminds? It uses most of GURPS logic, but is far better on my opinion. Simple and versatile, without adding so much mathematics to implement new mechanics (GURPS isn't heavy on base rules, but the advanced rules can go as far as to reach the realm of advanced Calculus, with the cost of a single advantage becoming a complex integer). I already run a Vampire chronicle in it, and it went pretty well.<br /> <br /> My own preference is for 2nd ed. M&amp;M along with Ultimate Power supplement. Everything else is just fluff and ideas on how to implement UP rules. You can try the 3rd ed. if you want, but I don't like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T18:23:21-08:00","id":1160718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160666#post1160666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, but first thats not how it works, it affects the perception stat which encompasses the 5 senses and applies to tracking. I don't get what you mean with &quot;Let the child of Gaia vulnerable to attack&quot; when i didn't mean a specific gift but a series of gift that do the same thing but render the previous ones redundant.<br /> <br /> And yes is an easy if taxing problem to solve just going through all the gift list and banning and fixing the redundant and/useless gifts which are more XP traps than anything else. Like the Gift to purify water.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I've noticed about OWoD, is there is a lot of ST discretion involved, at least from my experience with it. Blur of the Milky Eye does indeed say it affects Perception rolls, but the description of the Gift I feel matters just as much as the mechanic. The description says nothing about Sight or Sound in terms of what it's hiding, and when I run games, I would make it very clear that this Gift isn't going to hide them if someone can track easily via scent. A Vampire with high levels of Auspex, or a Garou with Heightened Senses on could potentially track via smell, or even heartbeat if that ended up being an easier roll than sight (Assuming someone rolls a ton of successes on Blur).<br /> <br /> Pure Breed is strong, for sure. But I also don't consider it super rare, other than very high levels of it. I often times give NPCs a dot or two of Pure Breed, since I feel like most Garou would not be so diluted as to have literally none left as the first dot essentially says &quot;You have your grandfather's eyes&quot; or something to that effect. I also make people &quot;justify&quot; their choices of backgrounds when making a character. If someone grabbed five points of Pure Breed simply because it's strong, there's a good chance I'd have to sit down and talk to them about the type of game I'm running. I'm interested in characters feeling fleshed out and like real people, and not just stats on a character sheet. Where as if they took a high level of Pure Breed, Ancestor, and Fetish, with the Reputation or Notable Heritage merit to signify that they're someone with a strong family heritage, and have an heirloom passed down from generation to generation, it would begin to feel more like a character and not just &quot;Pure Breed is really strong so I want it.&quot; I try to look at Stats, Skills, Merits, Flaws and Backgrounds as a whole. They're what make the character. There are definitely problems with the system, but I feel like a lot of the problems can be toned down if the ST is willing to talk to the players about why they're taking what they're taking, how it fits their concept and character, and if it feels like perhaps they're trying to get away with too much, simply saying &quot;Well, how about we tone this down just a little bit&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T19:09:59-08:00","id":1160732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160688#post1160688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, but I don't see many D&amp;D mechanics since 3rd edition being worse than most of WoD mechanics. If you think AD&amp;D, though, you didn't saw weird rules if you didn't saw TACH0.</div> </div> </div> </div>THAC0 is nothing before combat matrices, and 3.x was rife with such stinkers that the quickest path to a great degree of fair play was to ban the PHB classes from a game; so conceptually fouled that one could spend ages speaking of it, much like specialty priests ushering in CoDzilla. 5e also can't decide if monks should be a background or a class, and monks are quickly becoming the Asian Class.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless it is FATAL... </div> </div> </div>Can that really count as a game? It's really more of a collection of charts and racism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, <b>Saur Ops Specialist</b> already did a fine job describing how it will behave in GURPS. It is a nice system for its time, and you'll get rid of some problems, while having better tools to circumvent others (if you don't like multiple actions, implement other GURPS's mechanics to represent speed of action).<br /> <br /> But I think you'll be maybe better served by yet another system. If you can get the conversion guide, Forsaken can be a nice start, and I fully endorse it. But if you thought of GURPS, what about Mutants &amp; Masterminds? It uses most of GURPS logic, but is far better on my opinion. Simple and versatile, without adding so much mathematics to implement new mechanics (GURPS isn't heavy on base rules, but the advanced rules can go as far as to reach the realm of advanced Calculus, with the cost of a single advantage becoming a complex integer). I already run a Vampire chronicle in it, and it went pretty well. </div> </div> </div>Advanced rules in GURPS never require anything more than passing familiarity with Algebra 2 (maximizing an equation with only one variable is not even remotely comparable to third order integrals of an object to determine center of gravity as it loses mass due to multidirectional outflow), and that was only in 3E, and only with vehicles. 4e, from what I've heard, uses vastly simpler construction systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T19:24:10-08:00","id":1160740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vulcan7200</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160718#post1160718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pure Breed is strong, for sure. But I also don't consider it super rare, other than very high levels of it. I often times give NPCs a dot or two of Pure Breed, since I feel like most Garou would not be so diluted as to have literally none left as the first dot essentially says &quot;You have your grandfather's eyes&quot; or something to that effect. I also make people &quot;justify&quot; their choices of backgrounds when making a character. If someone grabbed five points of Pure Breed simply because it's strong, there's a good chance I'd have to sit down and talk to them about the type of game I'm running. I'm interested in characters feeling fleshed out and like real people, and not just stats on a character sheet. Where as if they took a high level of Pure Breed, Ancestor, and Fetish, with the Reputation or Notable Heritage merit to signify that they're someone with a strong family heritage, and have an heirloom passed down from generation to generation, it would begin to feel more like a character and not just &quot;Pure Breed is really strong so I want it.&quot; I try to look at Stats, Skills, Merits, Flaws and Backgrounds as a whole. They're what make the character. There are definitely problems with the system, but I feel like a lot of the problems can be toned down if the ST is willing to talk to the players about why they're taking what they're taking, how it fits their concept and character, and if it feels like perhaps they're trying to get away with too much, simply saying &quot;Well, how about we tone this down just a little bit&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue with that is there are tribes (like the fangs) in which having a high pure breed is required at chargen while in other is discouraged. Also as Purebreed doesn't necessarily have anything to do with &quot;your character&quot; in the sense that is not his actions that give him Purebreed. Any character could get 3/4 just by saying &quot;my character is a lost cub from an affair&quot;. It's something outside of the characters control.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And yes, I can rule 0 whatever rules </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">are</span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> bad but that doesn't mean they aren't bad. I can remove rolls to shape change and regenerate and make pure breed only factor in reproduction and not have any other bearance in the game but there is a point in which gotta think on throwing the whole system away.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160688#post1160688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think you'll be maybe better served by yet another system. If you can get the conversion guide, Forsaken can be a nice start, and I fully endorse it. But if you thought of GURPS, what about Mutants &amp; Masterminds? It uses most of GURPS logic, but is far better on my opinion. Simple and versatile, without adding so much mathematics to implement new mechanics (GURPS isn't heavy on base rules, but the advanced rules can go as far as to reach the realm of advanced Calculus, with the cost of a single advantage becoming a complex integer). I already run a Vampire chronicle in it, and it went pretty well.<br /> <br /> My own preference is for 2nd ed. M&amp;M along with Ultimate Power supplement. Everything else is just fluff and ideas on how to implement UP rules. You can try the 3rd ed. if you want, but I don't like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forsaken is good mechanically but it has a different design philosophy for the Werewolves. See, in Apocalypse an Elder Garou is a master/leader of his auspice. While in forsaken a character in the equivalent of rank 3 most likely mastered his auspice (5 renown) as he can raise the rest above it, and the ideal elder is a master of all renown as Father Wolf was the apex predator.<br /> <br /> Having DM Forsaken i found that many power are utterly useless unless you max renown. And all the Forsaken gifts are equivalent of a level 3. Meaning that the idea of going to the umbra to get a mighty gift is lost in forsaken.<br /> <br /> I havent read Mutants and Masterminds. Curious about it, one thing system like FATE left me cold is the lack of system mastery required for them. I like customization of character and small deal of system mastery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T22:01:09-08:00","id":1160767,"title":"","content":"GURPS Werewolf The Apocalypse and the other GURPS WOD ports, Mage and Vampire, were for GURPS 3e, maybe GURPS 3e revised or the compendium era GURPS 3rd edition (where Compendium I and II cleaned up the accumulated rules of many sourcebooks). The current edition of GURPS is GURPS 4e. There were substantial changes between GURPS 3e and GURPS 4e, including which switching hit points from Health to Strength as the base and revising many advantages. Fortunately, there are good conversion guides on the SJ Games websites.<br /> <br /> The more unusual material in Werewolf is going to convert less well, but without the restrictions on abilities (talents, skills, knowledges), it is easier to buy the GURPS skills and have the skills you want. The same is true with backgrounds. GURPS runs pretty smoothly if you limit the concepts because the main issue of GURPS is it does so many things. If you have a focus on the Werewolf elements, things will be more or less balanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T22:04:37-08:00","id":1160769,"title":"","content":"As for the GURPS ports of WoD books, I had all three back in the day. Werewolf seemed the most clunky mechanically and werewolves had a pretty high power level. Vampires weren't too hard to do, but the book added little to WoD other than the option to use GURPS mechanics. Mage worked ok and the skill options were so much better and there were actual rules for technology so that if you wanted a crazy future weapon, you just grabbed Ultra-Tech and had stats. I liked Mage best, but then Mage is my favorite White Wolf game by a large margin.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T00:09:39-08:00","id":1160782,"title":"","content":"Plus, the GURSP book is 1st ed based. Silver Fang albinos and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T02:54:21-08:00","id":1160788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160732#post1160732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can that really count as a game? It's really more of a collection of charts and racism.</div> </div> </div> </div>And rape, don't forget rape.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160732#post1160732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Advanced rules in GURPS never require anything more than passing familiarity with Algebra 2 (maximizing an equation with only one variable is not even remotely comparable to third order integrals of an object to determine center of gravity as it loses mass due to multidirectional outflow), and that was only in 3E, and only with vehicles. 4e, from what I've heard, uses vastly simpler construction systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that I saw something on the lines of third order integrals, but that was crazily advanced stuff. It is good to know that 4e simplified things. Either way, my pet peeve with GURPS isn't actually the math, but the excessive book keeping and arbitrary costs of everything. Not that other games aren't arbitrary, but GURPS is on an uncomfortable level for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160740#post1160740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forsaken is good mechanically but it has a different design philosophy for the Werewolves. See, in Apocalypse an Elder Garou is a master/leader of his auspice. While in forsaken a character in the equivalent of rank 3 most likely mastered his auspice (5 renown) as he can raise the rest above it, and the ideal elder is a master of all renown as Father Wolf was the apex predator.<br /> <br /> Having DM Forsaken i found that many power are utterly useless unless you max renown. And all the Forsaken gifts are equivalent of a level 3. Meaning that the idea of going to the umbra to get a mighty gift is lost in forsaken.<br /> <br /> I havent read Mutants and Masterminds. Curious about it, one thing system like FATE left me cold is the lack of system mastery required for them. I like customization of character and small deal of system mastery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you read Forsaken 2nd ed already? Maybe you'll like it more.<br /> <br /> But I know your worry, though I like FATE Accelerated for some games (more than FATE Core). For me, M&amp;M fits nicely in the amount of system mastery, and on the effects of it. I mean, it won't punish the player that is just starting and not minding much of the system, but still have a lot of tweaks and shit you can do when you know how. You can customize your character insanely, choose your preferred level of complexity on the sheet, and all that without going out of a core set of rules. I really recommend that you take your time to read just Core and Ultimate Power. In a sense, it is like Ascension in that every other book will just add thoughts to the material actually in those, since the system is just that flexible.<br /> <br /> Not saying that it is perfect, mind you, it does have its perks and downfalls like everything else, but seems to be in the right direction for what you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T07:52:51-08:00","id":1160847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160788#post1160788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And rape, don't forget rape.</div> </div> </div> </div>You want me to remember anything about FATAL, then it depends on what you pay.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm pretty sure that I saw something on the lines of third order integrals, but that was crazily advanced stuff. It is good to know that 4e simplified things. Either way, my pet peeve with GURPS isn't actually the math, but the excessive book keeping and arbitrary costs of everything. Not that other games aren't arbitrary, but GURPS is on an uncomfortable level for me. </div> </div> </div>No integral symbol has ever been part of a GURPS system. Anything that might have required it has already been simplified out, even in 3e, and calculated for you. Trust me, I have both the original and revised versions of Vehicles, as well as Robots. It's literally so simple that an elementary school kid can use it to make stuff (as I was in elementary school when I picked it up, and was not exactly mathematically inclined at the time, as opposed to my 20s, a time of learning about Green's Theorem, Stokes Theorem, and other lovely fluid dynamics calculations for atmospheric science at Georgia Tech). Said kid just needs a calculator or a spreadsheet application to keep track of all of the parts, because if there is one tedious thing about the construction system, it's the gob-smackingly long list of options available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T08:21:10-08:00","id":1160857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160666#post1160666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I made the Generation comparison because is often tough as one of the bad mechanics in Masquerade. Avatar if I remember correctly (had a similar issue) but only applied to the expenditure of quiessence (though i could be wrong, don't have the book with me now) it wasn't a social, political and combat stat all rolled in one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yes it is indeed powerful background in social and combat with Garou, but with noone else. While vampire generation and Mage Avatar affect a heavily core aspect of their games, their energy expediture at all times. Pure breed is more of a role playing element, powerful yes, but it can also cause trouble if the character won't hold tight to the high demands of his status, it can be a two edge knife.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160666#post1160666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Breaking the dice pool was an incredible punishing mechanic for one (having to use the lower of the 4 stats involved). Is a problem when a character can use 4 multi-action that with no penalty to those.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As I mentioned above it only causes trouble if you are anoyed by the long time it takes to end a round, since you have to add a lot of other elements, (attack, damage, soak, penalties etcetc). Having full dice in combat multi actions is not the problem, afterall you spend fuel to do so. All the othe rolls that make the round huge, I could agree to that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160666#post1160666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, but first thats not how it works, it affects the perception stat which encompasses the 5 senses and applies to tracking. I don't get what you mean with &quot;Let the child of Gaia vulnerable to attack&quot; when i didn't mean a specific gift but a series of gift that do the same thing but render the previous ones redundant.<br /> <br /> And yes is an easy if taxing problem to solve just going through all the gift list and banning and fixing the redundant and/useless gifts which are more XP traps than anything else. Like the Gift to purify water.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sorry but no, Blur of the milky eye affects only perception rolls based on sight, you know because of eye <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Because Perception covers the 5 senses it doesn't mean at all that a power that targets a character's perception affects all his senses. <br /> <br /> I will agree with you that there are indeed many gifts that are a buff up version of lower level ones and thats indeed an xp trap, children of gaia and shadow lords are good examples of this bad issue. But thats a major problem with tribe books, they have gifts that are allready in the core but in variations, which are unnesecary many times.<br /> <br /> But no Purify Water is a very useful gift, trust me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160666#post1160666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I understand how it works that why I wrote how it works. My point is that how it works is needlessly convoluted and you have kept all of that in your mind in each combat. Instead of all of that<br /> &quot;Garou always regenerate 1 bashing per turn, spend 1 gnosis to make it 1 lethal and eat Aggravated from Silver in all forms. Soak lethal in all&quot; less than a whole line vs your 2 entire lines of text. That's a better design.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may use the Dark Ages Revised Werewolf rule that allows werewolves soak lethal in breed form, they still don't regenerate. (less than 2 lines)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T10:22:41-08:00","id":1160902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160857#post1160857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]<br /> <br /> As I mentioned above it only causes trouble if you are anoyed by the long time it takes to end a round, since you have to add a lot of other elements, (attack, damage, soak, penalties etcetc). Having full dice in combat multi actions is not the problem, afterall you spend fuel to do so. All the othe rolls that make the round huge, I could agree to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its is a problem to me, i dislike the rocket tag nature of combat and before you suggest the usual excuse of &quot;Garou combat is suppose to be highly lethal realistically&quot; i will tell you that no, WOD never aims to be realistic and a rocket tag combat means that God stats are gonna appear. In this case initiative and/or dexterity.<br /> <br /> I dont have issue with multiaction be that the bad rules of multiaction (the using the lower of both dice rolls) or using the good rules of multiaction (mage revised) because in both each action after the previous one is gonna cost you.<br /> <br /> With Rage there is no downside to use them to gain extra actions beyond you got less rage and considering its get recharged in combat.<br /> <br /> I see a problem when a character start the first turn and land 4 attack with his full blown dicepool into a target because it either means i gotta TPK the entire party or just let them win by putting them enemies that dont use their rage to their full capacity.<br /> <br /> Okay, i get is not a problem to you. You might like the shitty system of WoD but i dont, and will try to change it for the better or throw away the whole rotten thing for a better system.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160857#post1160857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]<br /> [COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]<br /> You may use the Dark Ages Revised Werewolf rule that allows werewolves soak lethal in breed form, they still don't regenerate. (less than 2 lines)</div> </div> </div> </div>Your text is not clear in what they dont regenerate. So that whole &quot;less than 2 lines&quot; is not quite right and mine is the same lenght or less and still a better rule.<br /> <br /> What the point of not regenerating in breed form? Is yet another book keeping thing that add absolutely NOTHING to the game or setting.<br /> <br /> But i gotta ask what you point here? Because i open the thread asking about GURPS and you only keep defending OWoD system, which is neither here or there and is kinda pointless no of &quot;you can rule zero&quot; or &quot;its not as bad to me&quot; is gonna convince me that this system isnt as fragile as card house in a tornado, i play with the system enough on all the 3 lines.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160788#post1160788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you read Forsaken 2nd ed already? Maybe you'll like it more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was talking about 2nd edition forsaken. Most of the gift scale with renown and all are the equivalent of a level 3 gift.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160788#post1160788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really recommend that you take your time to read just Core and Ultimate Power. In a sense, it is like Ascension in that every other book will just add thoughts to the material actually in those, since the system is just that flexible.<br /> <br /> Not saying that it is perfect, mind you, it does have its perks and downfalls like everything else, but seems to be in the right direction for what you want.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160847#post1160847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Said kid just needs a calculator or a spreadsheet application to keep track of all of the parts, because if there is one tedious thing about the construction system, it's the gob-smackingly long list of options available.</div> </div> </div> </div>So is GURPS 4E that dependant on hex maps? Or is there a supplement for lets say &quot;narrative movement&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160769#post1160769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the GURPS ports of WoD books, I had all three back in the day. Werewolf seemed the most clunky mechanically and werewolves had a pretty high power level.</div> </div> </div> </div>So why were they clunky? Because they were powerful compared to humans or it had other issues?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-20-2017, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T10:56:06-08:00","id":1160911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160902#post1160902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is GURPS 4E that dependant on hex maps? Or is there a supplement for lets say &quot;narrative movement&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically no, in that you can wing it by declaring how far away something is, but I don't know of a narrative movement system for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T14:26:46-08:00","id":1160968,"title":"","content":"Narrative movement is a rare thing, not even the WoD books use it. But generally you can keep things flowing just stating distances on most system. I almost never use grids even in D&amp;D 4th ed.<br /> <br /> But GURPS is proud of the level of detail you can put in the system, so if your players are picky with this sort of things, wanting to take advantage on each feet of movement they can at a turn, be prepared for the hex grid. If you have no such players, then you'll be ok without it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T16:51:10-08:00","id":1161005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160968#post1160968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Narrative movement is a rare thing, not even the WoD books use it. But generally you can keep things flowing just stating distances on most system. I almost never use grids even in D&amp;D 4th ed.<br /> <br /> But GURPS is proud of the level of detail you can put in the system, so if your players are picky with this sort of things, wanting to take advantage on each feet of movement they can at a turn, be prepared for the hex grid. If you have no such players, then you'll be ok without it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yards. By default, it works in yards. A foot is only one third of the way through a hex. Even GURPS has limits on how much detail it can keep in focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T17:00:34-08:00","id":1161006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1160902#post1160902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So is GURPS 4E that dependant on hex maps? Or is there a supplement for lets say &quot;narrative movement&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So why were they clunky? Because they were powerful compared to humans or it had other issues?</div> </div> </div> </div>GURPS also has range band options if you prefer to use abstracted ranges. You don't really need hex maps to play. Basically, you just need range to figure out the attack modifiers for ranged attacks. Yards are close enough to meters if you are a metric person to use metric maps unless you really want to crunch the difference.<br /> <br /> As for the clunkiness of Werewolf, it was more how the port felt. WoD games have fairly simple mechanics and a WTA werewolf in GURPS was a big list of abilities. Also, some of the mechanics didn't translate into easy explanations and because this was GURPS 3e days, they balanced less with other material than things do in GURPS 4e days. A base werewolf is more powerful than a human, but built on the same point total, you could make some awesome humans. Werewolves were at least 300 point characters, IIRC. Mages and vampires were pretty buff, too.<br /> <br /> If you like the GURPS mechanics more than WoD and are willing to do some work, the GURPS Werewolf the Apocalypse book could be worth it for you. I just feel that it was the less effective of the three ports at capturing the original game. . .<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T18:31:11-08:00","id":1161032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1161006#post1161006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> GURPS also has range band options if you prefer to use abstracted ranges. You don't really need hex maps to play. Basically, you just need range to figure out the attack modifiers for ranged attacks. Yards are close enough to meters if you are a metric person to use metric maps unless you really want to crunch the difference.<br /> <br /> As for the clunkiness of Werewolf, it was more how the port felt. WoD games have fairly simple mechanics and a WTA werewolf in GURPS was a big list of abilities. Also, some of the mechanics didn't translate into easy explanations and because this was GURPS 3e days, they balanced less with other material than things do in GURPS 4e days. A base werewolf is more powerful than a human, but built on the same point total, you could make some awesome humans. Werewolves were at least 300 point characters, IIRC. Mages and vampires were pretty buff, too.<br /> <br /> If you like the GURPS mechanics more than WoD and are willing to do some work, the GURPS Werewolf the Apocalypse book could be worth it for you. I just feel that it was the less effective of the three ports at capturing the original game. . .<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>More like 700+ point characters. The Garou package of capabilities is extremely costly, even when people run the numbers on 4e conversions, where Strength and Health cost less, along with a number of advantages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T14:30:59-08:00","id":1161281,"title":"","content":"No wonder they were unplayable. 700 points in GURPS 3e was pretty much demigod level, as 300 was low-level supers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T17:10:00-08:00","id":1161342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1161281#post1161281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No wonder they were unplayable. 700 points in GURPS 3e was pretty much demigod level, as 300 was low-level supers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Higher point totals doesn't produce unplayability by default, it just means that your character is the peer of some of the nastier stuff from GURPS Monsters, which is as it should be, since you are, after all, playing one of the most powerful forms of werewolf there is in fiction. Also, if you convert over ST system characters built the way most vampires, werewolves, etc. are, you'd come away with some pretty high point totals just from characters who maxed out their DX and IQ; five dots being the equivalent of 20, that means someone with Dex and Int at 5 dots each is a 400 point character just from those stat totals. Earlier editions would have valued Strength and Health in a similar capacity. Just having maxed out Attributes does not a demigod make.<br /> <br /> Also, let's be serious, 300 points is so low-powered for most Supers games that it'd likely be more of a pulp game, and possibly not even a high-end one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T17:53:01-08:00","id":1161357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1161342#post1161342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Higher point totals doesn't produce unplayability by default, it just means that your character is the peer of some of the nastier stuff from GURPS Monsters, which is as it should be, since you are, after all, playing one of the most powerful forms of werewolf there is in fiction. Also, if you convert over ST system characters built the way most vampires, werewolves, etc. are, you'd come away with some pretty high point totals just from characters who maxed out their DX and IQ; five dots being the equivalent of 20, that means someone with Dex and Int at 5 dots each is a 400 point character just from those stat totals. Earlier editions would have valued Strength and Health in a similar capacity. Just having maxed out Attributes does not a demigod make.<br /> <br /> Also, let's be serious, 300 points is so low-powered for most Supers games that it'd likely be more of a pulp game, and possibly not even a high-end one.</div> </div> </div> </div>So lets assume i wanna run a game with just Werwolves, humans, spirits, fomoris and banes. No crossover, no robots? The power points are not that much of an issue arent they?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T20:12:43-08:00","id":1161401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1160409-gurps-werewolf-is-it-worth-it?p=1161357#post1161357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So lets assume i wanna run a game with just Werwolves, humans, spirits, fomoris and banes. No crossover, no robots?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, mainline Werewolf still has robots and cyborgs in it. Also, statting out spirits, as I've noted, can still be a pain, but you don't really need to adhere to point totals that closely if they aren't PCs, I suppose. Adjudicating how some Charms work may also be a pain, but I've not looked at how it handled those in a long, long time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The power points are not that much of an issue arent they? </div> </div> </div>Not really. Though, as noted, converting characters over from ST stats to GURPS is going to result in some pretty high point totals, even for normal humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T17:50:58-08:00","id":1162295,"title":"","content":"Mostly you'll have to closely watch your PCs building their sheets. As a point-based system, it gives so much freedom in character creation that you can easily end up with fairly unexpected results. It isn't unbalanced or such, but the system itself won't keep your players from getting something you planned as a 5th level Gift from start. Discuss your plans to the chronicle, and heard theirs with extra care just to be on the same page.<br /> <br /> You don't need to keep tabs on how much the monsters, minions and NPCs cost on points. But they being 700 points characters mean they have an extremely broad variety of possible sheets. The Garou Template will simplify things a little, but you can still end up with characters far more specialized than you're used to on WoD. Again, just be in the same page as them.<br /> <br /> The same is true for M&amp;M, though I still think it is easier for the task at hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}